  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of emergency health and protection response and ensuring the access of the community (including those affected by the quake) to health</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will prioritize maintaining the functionality of a critical Comprehensive Emergency Obstetric and Neonatal care (CEmONC) hospital and a primary health care (PHC) center, through supporting Al-Farabi hospital for four months and Kafrehmul center for six months  , as they are out of support, and consequently, securing the introduction of life saving service delivery by the provision of basic health services, procurement of medical supplies and fuel.SEMA will also support a community center (CC) in Salqin, introducing both child protection and gender-based-violence (GBV) case management services, legal counseling, in addition to PFA, and outreach activities through adopting the emergency response model (ERM) , to achieve rapid success as this approach has proved its effectiveness in reaching beneficiaries during emergency situations and ensuring their access to service.</narrative>
  </description>
